  data: {
    LLM: "Fold early. If your hole card and first up-card don't form at least a high pair or a very strong high-card combination, you should rarely see the third card.\n\nThe 'Upcard' Check: Always look at EVERY upcard on the table. If you are drawing for a Flush in Hearts, and you see three other Heart cards in your opponents' upcards, your odds of completing your hand are significantly reduced.\n\nRepresenting a Hand: If you have a high upcard (like an Ace or King), you can bet aggressively to represent a 'Pair of Aces'. Opponents must respect the possibility that your hole card matches your visible high card.",
    Player: "Fold early. If your hole card and first up-card don't form at least a high pair or a very strong high-card combination, you should rarely see the third card.\n\nThe 'Upcard' Check: Always look at EVERY upcard on the table. If you are drawing for a Flush in Hearts, and you see three other Heart cards in your opponents' upcards, your odds of completing your hand are significantly reduced.\n\nRepresenting a Hand: If you have a high upcard (like an Ace or King), you can bet aggressively to represent a 'Pair of Aces'. Opponents must respect the possibility that your hole card matches your visible high card.",
